Currently we are trying to keep an aspect ratio of 16:9 as this is the standard resolution of most monitors. 


## Panel Sizes

This means that with our current double layer of 16:9, we will need to double the width of the screen. This means adding 2 panes to either side with a total width of 320. In addition we will need to add a pane at the top and the bottom for controls. This means that the sides and the top need to be updated by n.

So to get the sizes of each of the panes we will need to: 

Left Pane: 320:540
Right Pane: 320:
This will make the resulting dimensions

Width:  320+320+320     = 960
Height: 180+180+60+60   = 540

960:540 = 16:9


